{"parentUuid":"c41b9317-3339-4730-9748-a1e309774a8b","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/app/workspace","sessionId":"f0f8cf3a-addc-49b6-ad31-e331452c2b8b","version":"2.1.19","gitBranch":"","slug":"inherited-spinning-whale","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_vrtx_0185oyR32MP53jWVV7kz9DSe","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Excellent! Let me compile all the information I've gathered into a comprehensive response.\n\n## Summary\n\nBased on my research of the official Google cluster-data documentation and related sources, here's the schema for the Google cluster-usage traces dataset (ClusterData2011_2):\n\n### TASK_EVENTS Schema\n\nThe task_events CSV table contains the following columns (in order):\n\n| Column # | Column Name | Data Type | Description |\n|-----------|------------|-----------|-------------|\n| 1 | timestamp | int64 | Unix timestamp in microseconds since the start of the trace |\n| 2 | missing_data | int/bool | Indicates if some data is missing for this record (0/1) |\n| 3 | job_id | int64 | Unique identifier for the parent job |\n| 4 | task_index | int | 0-based task index within the job |\n| 5 | machine_id | int64 | Machine identifier where task is scheduled (empty if not scheduled) |\n| 6 | event_type | int | Type of event (0=SUBMIT, 1=SCHEDULE, 2=EVICT, 3=FAIL, 4=FINISH, 5=KILL, 6=LOST, 7=UPDATE_PENDING, 8=UPDATE_RUNNING) |\n| 7 | user | string | Obfuscated username/service identifier |\n| 8 | scheduling_class | int | Latency sensitivity classification (0=free, 1=batch, 2=best_effort, 3=interactive) |\n| 9 | priority | int | Task priority (0-11, where 0-1=free, 9-11=production) |\n| 10 | cpu_requested | float | CPU cores requested for the task |\n| 11 | memory_requested | float | Memory (GB) requested for the task |\n| 12 | disk_requested | float | Disk space requested for the task |\n| 13 | different_machines_restriction | int/bool | Whether task must run on different machine (0/1) |\n\n### JOB_EVENTS Schema\n\nThe job_events CSV table contains the following columns:\n\n| Column # | Column Name | Data Type | Description |\n|-----------|------------|-----------|-------------|\n| 1 | timestamp | int64 | Unix timestamp in microseconds since the start of the trace |\n| 2 | missing_data | int/bool | Indicates if some data is missing for this record (0/1) |\n| 3 | job_id | int64 | Unique identifier for the job |\n| 4 | event_type | int | Type of event (0=SUBMIT, 1=SCHEDULE, 2=EVICT, 3=FAIL, 4=FINISH, 5=KILL, 6=LOST, 7=UPDATE_PENDING, 8=UPDATE_RUNNING) |\n| 5 | scheduling_class | int | Latency sensitivity classification |\n| 6 | user | string | Obfuscated username/service identifier |\n| 7 | job_name_hash | string | Obfuscated job name |\n| 8 | logical_job_name_hash | string | Obfuscated logical job name |\n\n### Key Characteristics\n\n- **Format**: CSV with Unix-style line endings (ASCII LF), no headers\n- **Timestamp**: Microseconds since trace start (May 1, 2011 19:00 EDT)\n- **Missing Data**: Approximately 0.013% of task events and 0.0008% of job events have non-empty missing data fields\n- **Boolean Fields**: Represented as 0 (false) or 1 (true)\n- **Empty Fields**: If a field has no value, the field is left empty in the CSV\n- **File Splitting**: Large tables are split into numbered files; records are never split across files\n- **Data Size**: Compressed trace is approximately 41GB\n\n### Your Sample Data Analysis\n\nLooking at your task_events sample:\n```\n5611824441,,6251812952,1761,1306108,4,fJYeclskJqPWsAT6TX/r9X5OiIZpSEb2PBGliYAOMxM=,0,2,0.02499,0.07959,0.0003862,1\n```\n\nBreaking it down:\n- timestamp: 5611824441\n- missing_data: (empty)\n- job_id: 6251812952\n- task_index: 1761\n- machine_id: 1306108\n- event_type: 4 (FINISH)\n- user: fJYeclskJqPWsAT6TX/r9X5OiIZpSEb2PBGliYAOMxM= (obfuscated)\n- scheduling_class: 0\n- priority: 2\n- cpu_requested: 0.02499\n- memory_requested: 0.07959\n- disk_requested: 0.0003862\n- different_machines_restriction: 1\n\nSources:\n- [Google Cluster Data GitHub Repository](https://github.com/google/cluster-data)\n- [ClusterData2011_2 Documentation](https://github.com/google/cluster-data/blob/master/ClusterData2011_2.md)\n- [First Steps Exploring the Google Cluster Dataset](https://stillwell.me/~mark/post/first-steps-exploring-the-google-cluster-dataset-with-ipython/)\n- [Analysis and Clustering of Workload in Google Cluster Trace](https://arxiv.org/pdf/1501.01426)\n- [A Deep Dive into the Google Cluster Workload Traces](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2308.02358)\n- [Google Cluster Trace Dataset Overview](https://www.emergentmind.com/topics/google-cluster-trace-dataset)"},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: a4efa48 (for resuming to continue this agent's work if needed)"}]}]},"uuid":"f912e953-63f1-401b-a356-70c2d925b076","timestamp":"2026-01-29T06:25:59.185Z","toolUseResult":{"status":"completed","prompt":"I need to understand the schema of Google cluster-usage traces dataset. I have sample CSV data:\n\nTask events sample:\n```\n5611824441,,6251812952,1761,1306108,4,fJYeclskJqPWsAT6TX/r9X5OiIZpSEb2PBGliYAOMxM=,0,2,0.02499,0.07959,0.0003862,1\n```\n\nJob events sample:\n```\n5620274759,,6252007148,4,AL1ptJgzhEaoLf97k5xU6Uc2VO0yUaPQd/feJ5LMWhA=,0,v9ts2JYvO1mIA0WIprzcfG/VuLV2+k4Q7RBlLP47TiI=,8eJUX2smexw6vuP11WVFleSoOZQT7UEsTxYigrSyMjw=\n```\n\nFrom the ClusterData2011_2 documentation, I know this is a Google cluster-usage traces dataset from May 2011. The data includes timestamps in microseconds.\n\nCan you find the official schema for these CSV files? Search for \"Google cluster-usage traces CSV schema\", \"Google Borg cluster trace format\", or similar. I need to know the column names and types for both task_events and job_events CSV files.","agentId":"a4efa48","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Excellent! Let me compile all the information I've gathered into a comprehensive response.\n\n## Summary\n\nBased on my research of the official Google cluster-data documentation and related sources, here's the schema for the Google cluster-usage traces dataset (ClusterData2011_2):\n\n### TASK_EVENTS Schema\n\nThe task_events CSV table contains the following columns (in order):\n\n| Column # | Column Name | Data Type | Description |\n|-----------|------------|-----------|-------------|\n| 1 | timestamp | int64 | Unix timestamp in microseconds since the start of the trace |\n| 2 | missing_data | int/bool | Indicates if some data is missing for this record (0/1) |\n| 3 | job_id | int64 | Unique identifier for the parent job |\n| 4 | task_index | int | 0-based task index within the job |\n| 5 | machine_id | int64 | Machine identifier where task is scheduled (empty if not scheduled) |\n| 6 | event_type | int | Type of event (0=SUBMIT, 1=SCHEDULE, 2=EVICT, 3=FAIL, 4=FINISH, 5=KILL, 6=LOST, 7=UPDATE_PENDING, 8=UPDATE_RUNNING) |\n| 7 | user | string | Obfuscated username/service identifier |\n| 8 | scheduling_class | int | Latency sensitivity classification (0=free, 1=batch, 2=best_effort, 3=interactive) |\n| 9 | priority | int | Task priority (0-11, where 0-1=free, 9-11=production) |\n| 10 | cpu_requested | float | CPU cores requested for the task |\n| 11 | memory_requested | float | Memory (GB) requested for the task |\n| 12 | disk_requested | float | Disk space requested for the task |\n| 13 | different_machines_restriction | int/bool | Whether task must run on different machine (0/1) |\n\n### JOB_EVENTS Schema\n\nThe job_events CSV table contains the following columns:\n\n| Column # | Column Name | Data Type | Description |\n|-----------|------------|-----------|-------------|\n| 1 | timestamp | int64 | Unix timestamp in microseconds since the start of the trace |\n| 2 | missing_data | int/bool | Indicates if some data is missing for this record (0/1) |\n| 3 | job_id | int64 | Unique identifier for the job |\n| 4 | event_type | int | Type of event (0=SUBMIT, 1=SCHEDULE, 2=EVICT, 3=FAIL, 4=FINISH, 5=KILL, 6=LOST, 7=UPDATE_PENDING, 8=UPDATE_RUNNING) |\n| 5 | scheduling_class | int | Latency sensitivity classification |\n| 6 | user | string | Obfuscated username/service identifier |\n| 7 | job_name_hash | string | Obfuscated job name |\n| 8 | logical_job_name_hash | string | Obfuscated logical job name |\n\n### Key Characteristics\n\n- **Format**: CSV with Unix-style line endings (ASCII LF), no headers\n- **Timestamp**: Microseconds since trace start (May 1, 2011 19:00 EDT)\n- **Missing Data**: Approximately 0.013% of task events and 0.0008% of job events have non-empty missing data fields\n- **Boolean Fields**: Represented as 0 (false) or 1 (true)\n- **Empty Fields**: If a field has no value, the field is left empty in the CSV\n- **File Splitting**: Large tables are split into numbered files; records are never split across files\n- **Data Size**: Compressed trace is approximately 41GB\n\n### Your Sample Data Analysis\n\nLooking at your task_events sample:\n```\n5611824441,,6251812952,1761,1306108,4,fJYeclskJqPWsAT6TX/r9X5OiIZpSEb2PBGliYAOMxM=,0,2,0.02499,0.07959,0.0003862,1\n```\n\nBreaking it down:\n- timestamp: 5611824441\n- missing_data: (empty)\n- job_id: 6251812952\n- task_index: 1761\n- machine_id: 1306108\n- event_type: 4 (FINISH)\n- user: fJYeclskJqPWsAT6TX/r9X5OiIZpSEb2PBGliYAOMxM= (obfuscated)\n- scheduling_class: 0\n- priority: 2\n- cpu_requested: 0.02499\n- memory_requested: 0.07959\n- disk_requested: 0.0003862\n- different_machines_restriction: 1\n\nSources:\n- [Google Cluster Data GitHub Repository](https://github.com/google/cluster-data)\n- [ClusterData2011_2 Documentation](https://github.com/google/cluster-data/blob/master/ClusterData2011_2.md)\n- [First Steps Exploring the Google Cluster Dataset](https://stillwell.me/~mark/post/first-steps-exploring-the-google-cluster-dataset-with-ipython/)\n- [Analysis and Clustering of Workload in Google Cluster Trace](https://arxiv.org/pdf/1501.01426)\n- [A Deep Dive into the Google Cluster Workload Traces](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2308.02358)\n- [Google Cluster Trace Dataset Overview](https://www.emergentmind.com/topics/google-cluster-trace-dataset)"}],"totalDurationMs":121146,"totalTokens":28064,"totalToolUseCount":22,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":302,"cache_read_input_tokens":27756,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":302,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":6}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c41b9317-3339-4730-9748-a1e309774a8b"}
